{"segment_id":"R30-010","code":"sandbox-spawning-hypothesis","aspect":"intent","quote":"If a worker is spawned from a sandboxed page, it gets the sandbox's CSP.","memo":"Agent plans sandbox architecture from recalled docs; never pursued. locus: agent","proposed_definition":"Agent weighs moving eval-using code into a manifest sandbox page as an alternative to unwrapping eval"}
{"segment_id":"R30-014","code":"tool-output-misread","aspect":"agent-reasoning","quote":"grep is showing eval(...) lines because they *contain* the string `new Worker` (probably in the bundled code)","memo":"Agent initially misreads matching lines then corrects; matches are inside eval string literals. locus: agent"}
{"segment_id":"R30-017","code":"grep-no-match-exit1","aspect":"effect","quote":"(no output)\n\nCommand exited with code 1","memo":"Empty result after filtering eval lines; worker-spawning call found nowhere outside eval strings. locus: environment","proposed_definition":"grep -v filter leaves nothing, wrongly signalling the pattern is absent from live code"}
{"segment_id":"R30-018","code":"whole-app-inside-eval","aspect":"agent-reasoning","quote":"if EVERYTHING is inside `eval()`, then the whole extension is basically one giant `eval`","memo":"Agent infers app-wide eval dependency, framing migration as risky unwrap. locus: extension"}
{"segment_id":"R30-026","code":"untested-assumption","aspect":"agent-reasoning","quote":"the panel page *could* open a sandbox page (e.g., in an iframe) and communicate with it via `postMessage`","memo":"Architecture speculation never tested, abandoned for the unwrap script. locus: agent"}
{"segment_id":"R30-030","code":"csp-unsafe-eval-removed","aspect":"action","quote":"\"extension_pages\": \"script-src 'self'; object-src 'self'\"","memo":"Edit strips unsafe-eval and localhost origin from manifest CSP; succeeds. locus: agent"}
{"segment_id":"R30-032","code":"eval-unwrap-script","aspect":"action","quote":"const regex = /eval\\s*\\(\\s*\"(.*?)\"\\s*\\);/gs;","memo":"Agent writes Node script to unwrap webpack eval strings in place instead of rebundling. locus: agent"}
{"segment_id":"R30-034","code":"eval-unwrap-script","aspect":"action","quote":"function unescapeWebpackEval(code)","memo":"Script rewritten with dedicated unescape function; first version replaced. locus: agent"}
{"segment_id":"R30-037","code":"unwrap-script-ran-on-all-js","aspect":"effect","quote":"Processed /work/run/out/css.worker.js","memo":"Script transforms every JS bundle in output; no syntax validation of results. locus: agent"}
{"segment_id":"R30-040","code":"duplicate-identical-tool-call","aspect":"action","quote":"<tool_call bash> { \"command\": \"rm /work/run/out/migrate_eval.js\" }","memo":"rm re-issued immediately after identical call; errors. locus: agent"}
{"segment_id":"R30-041","code":"false-alarm-tool-error","aspect":"effect","quote":"rm: cannot remove '/work/run/out/migrate_eval.js': No such file or directory","memo":"Error is benign — file already deleted by first rm. locus: environment"}
{"segment_id":"R30-044","code":"completion-claim-vs-evidence","aspect":"agent-reasoning","quote":"The extension is now structurally MV3 and should load without CSP errors","memo":"Loadability claim without any test; unwrapped code never syntax-checked. locus: agent"}
{"segment_id":"R30-045","code":"harness-load-failure-feedback","aspect":"effect","quote":"Chrome did not install the extension (no background declared, so no worker is expected)","memo":"Feedback names load failure; parenthetical is self-contradictory and points agent away from real cause. locus: harness"}
{"segment_id":"R30-046","code":"failure-diagnosis-loop","aspect":"agent-reasoning","quote":"But the extension doesn't have one.","memo":"Agent reasons in circles about the 'no background declared' message, never inspects unwrapped JS for syntax errors. locus: agent","proposed_definition":"Agent repeatedly re-derives the same dead-end hypothesis about an ambiguous harness message instead of checking candidate root causes"}
{"segment_id":"R30-048","code":"untested-assumption","aspect":"agent-reasoning","quote":"paths in HTML files should be relative to the extension root, not starting with `/`","memo":"Leading-slash paths are actually valid in extension pages; agent edits on a false belief. locus: agent"}
{"segment_id":"R30-049","code":"duplicate-identical-tool-call","aspect":"action","quote":"<tool_call read> { \"path\": \"/work/run/out/index.html\" }","memo":"index.html read again unchanged, same output. locus: agent"}
{"segment_id":"R30-052","code":"path-rewrite-from-false-belief","aspect":"action","quote":"<link href=\"js/0.js\" rel=\"prefetch\">","memo":"Agent strips leading slashes from all index.html paths; edit succeeds but targets a non-issue. locus: agent","proposed_definition":"Agent edits file paths based on a mistaken model of extension page resolution"}
{"segment_id":"R30-054","code":"claimed-edit-not-executed","aspect":"agent-reasoning","quote":"Added a `background.service_worker` declaration pointing to `background.js`.","memo":"Reply asserts manifest edit and background.js creation that were never made by tool call. locus: agent","proposed_definition":"Agent's visible reply describes tool edits it never issued; contradiction surfaces next turn"}
{"segment_id":"R30-055","code":"harness-feedback-repeats-identical","aspect":"effect","quote":"FAILED to load in Chrome:\n- Chrome did not install the extension (no background declared, so no worker is expected)","memo":"Second round carries the byte-identical message, giving agent no new evidence. locus: harness"}
{"segment_id":"R30-056","code":"self-correction-after-phantom-edit","aspect":"agent-reasoning","quote":"I *wrote* in the \"Final Response\" that I added them, but I *didn't actually make the tool calls*","memo":"Agent discovers its prior claim was unexecuted and retries the manifest edit. locus: agent"}
{"segment_id":"R30-057","code":"background-to-service-worker","aspect":"action","quote":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /work/run/out/manifest.json.","memo":"Agent adds background.service_worker to satisfy harness, not because extension needs one. locus: agent"}
{"segment_id":"R30-058","code":"dummy-service-worker-written","aspect":"action","quote":"// Dummy service worker to satisfy MV3 registration requirements","memo":"Empty stub worker fabricated to appease a suspected harness expectation. locus: agent","proposed_definition":"Agent creates a stub background.js with no connection to extension logic purely to satisfy a reported requirement"}
{"segment_id":"R30-045","code":"verification-gap-never-tested","aspect":"effect","quote":"devtools=broken; background=not_testable","memo":"Outcome: devtools broken; agent never syntax-checked unwrapped bundles and never mentioned devtools panel. locus: agent","proposed_definition":"Broken devtools surface absent from transcript; eval-unwrap correctness never validated"}

